sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/approach/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia--claude-opus-5-5--1> a prov:Plan, delphi:TestableHypothesis ;
    rdfs:label "Computer-assisted proof that Weaire–Phelan is a strict local minimum among periodic foams" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia> ;
    dct:description "Prove local optimality of the Weaire–Phelan (WP) partition within its periodic class, the result the problem asks for. Setting: partitions of the 3-torus ℝ³/Λ (the WP cubic cell, 8 cells) into cells of equal volume. WP's faces are constant-mean-curvature surfaces meeting at Plateau angles. Plan: (a) compute the WP equilibrium with Surface Evolver at high refinement with an a-posteriori error bound; (b) compute the second variation (the Jacobi operator on faces with the Plateau-border coupling conditions and volume constraints) discretized by finite elements; (c) certify, with interval arithmetic in Arb, a lower bound λ_min > 0 on the constrained Hessian's smallest non-trivial eigenvalue, modulo translations, using a residual-based enclosure (Kato–Temple or Lehmann–Goerisch bounds) that converts discrete eigenvalue estimates into rigorous bounds for the continuous operator. A positive bound proves WP is a strict local minimum against all smooth volume-preserving perturbations periodic on Λ. The same pipeline applied to Kelvin's foam reproduces known stability as a validation." ;

    delphi:proposedTest "A certified bound λ_min > 0 for WP's constrained second variation on its periodic cell, proving strict local optimality among equal-volume partitions with that period, the first rigorous optimality-type statement for WP." ;
    delphi:context "Fails if: The discrete-to-continuous error bound for curved faces with Plateau-border junctions cannot be made rigorous with available eigenvalue-enclosure methods, or the certified margin is negative within error, leaving the result unproved." ;
    delphi:hypothesisType "approach/proof" ;
    skos:note "Steps: 1. Compute WP and Kelvin equilibria in Surface Evolver; validate surface areas against published values (Kelvin 5.306, WP 5.288 in units of V^(2/3) for total cell surface). 2. Discretize the constrained second variation; compute the lowest eigenvalues numerically. 3. Derive rigorous eigenvalue lower bounds with Lehmann–Goerisch and Arb interval arithmetic. 4. Validate on Kelvin; publish the certificate and code." ;
    skos:note "Difficulty (proposer's estimate of completion within about a month of agent time): long-shot" ;
    skos:note "Missing: Rigorous spectral enclosure for operators on foam networks with singular junction lines is research-level numerical analysis." ;
    skos:note "Tool: surface-evolver" ;
    skos:note "Tool: interval-arithmetic" ;
    skos:note "Tool: finite-element-analysis" ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-04> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-11> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch07-08> ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch09-16> ;

    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1080/09500839408241577> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://doi.org/10.1080/10586458.1992.10504253> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://kenbrakke.com/evolver/evolver.html> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://arblib.org/> ;
    rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://github.com/fractastical/delphi/blob/ee98025a1960b300fcc06aa2106f51118b60f565/problems/approaches/claude-opus-5-5.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/problem/kelvin-problem-in-epithelia> a delphi:Concept, schema:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Kelvin's problem in epithelia" .


  <https://doi.org/10.1080/09500839408241577> dct:title "A counter-example to Kelvin's conjecture on minimal surfaces" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Weaire and Phelan 1994, A counter-example to Kelvin's conjecture on minimal surfaces" .
  <https://doi.org/10.1080/10586458.1992.10504253> dct:title "The Surface Evolver" ;
    dct:bibliographicCitation "Brakke 1992, The Surface Evolver" .
  <https://kenbrakke.com/evolver/evolver.html> dct:bibliographicCitation "Surface Evolver software" .
  <https://arblib.org/> dct:bibliographicCitation "Arb ball arithmetic" .
}

